# Cloudflare static-asset redirects. One rule per line, first match wins.
# Copied verbatim into dist/client/ by the build; the Cloudflare adapter
# appends any Astro-declared redirects underneath.

# No www rule here, and none is possible (checked against
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/redirects/,
# last updated 2026-08-25, read 2026-09-10). A rule's source must be
# "A file path" — only the destination may be "A file path or external link" —
# and the Advanced redirects table lists "Domain-level redirects" as ❌, with
# `workers.example.com/* workers.example.com/blog/:splat 301` as the example
# that does not work. wrangler.toml attaches both macmladen.com and
# www.macmladen.com to this Worker as custom domains, so www serves the site
# and a zone-level Redirect Rule (created via the API, 2026-09-10) sends it to
# the apex with a 301; see ROADMAP.md.

# Short, sayable aliases for the workshop, for a slide or a spoken URL.
# Temporary on purpose: /speaking/<year>/<event-slug>/ is the canonical home
# of every appearance, so next year these two point somewhere else.
/radionica  /speaking/2026/wordcamp-belgrade-ddev-ai/  302
/workshop   /speaking/2026/wordcamp-belgrade-ddev-ai/  302

# The slash-less and the legacy Jekyll form of /about/. Cloudflare's default
# html_handling ("auto-trailing-slash", which the adapter leaves alone) would
# already send /about to /about/, but as a 307; the spec says 301, and a
# permanent redirect is what a URL that moved once and will not move again
# deserves. Redirect rules are evaluated before assets are served, so these
# win over that default. /about/ itself matches neither rule and is served
# normally.
/about      /about/  301
/about.html /about/  301
